
This package contains the following pre-built non-Greenplum software:

  R        - http://www.r-project.org/

  Each of which are covered by their own licenses.



The following commands show how to install the packages in this zip file.

All commands listed below are to be run as the gpadmin user on the master
host.

Stop the database:
gpstop -a

Run this script to modify where R will find it's libraries (The R install location must be provided):
./modify-R-startup-path.sh <R-install-location>

Install "R" on all segment hosts into a directory (<R-install-location>):
gpscp -rf <host-file> R =:<R-install-location>

Edit the file $GPHOME/greenplum_path.sh and append the following line:
export R_HOME=<R-install-location/lib>
 
Distribute changes to all segments
gpscp $GPHOME/greenplum_path.sh =:$GPHOME
 
Source the new greenplum_path.sh
. $GPHOME/greenplum_path.sh
 
Start the database:
gpstart -a
 
Connect to the database you wish to install to
psql <database-name>
 
Install PL/R:
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
CHANGEME: The path of plr.sql needs to reflect where the file is in $GPHOME
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
\i sql/plr.sql
